              "file": "experiments/ml-ensemble-extremes/20261018-0059-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/97773b52/record.json",
              "patch": "Index: experiments/ml-ensemble-extremes/20261018-0059-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/97773b52/record.json\n===================================================================\n--- experiments/ml-ensemble-extremes/20261018-0059-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/97773b52/record.json\t\n+++ experiments/ml-ensemble-extremes/20261018-0059-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/97773b52/record.json\t\n@@ -0,0 +1,181 @@\n+{\n+  \"option_title\": \"Ensemble size for rare extremes in a machine-learned weather ensemble\",\n+  \"question\": \"Does 10 to 1,000 AIFS-ENS members beat 50 for top-percentile wind, temperature, and rain probability forecasts, or does shared model error cap the skill?\",\n+  \"hypothesis\": \"More members keep helping: 1,000 members sample top-percentile tails far better than 50, so extreme-event scores keep improving [s_hens].\",\n+  \"compute_axis\": {\n+    \"quantity\": \"ensemble members per forecast\",\n+    \"unit\": \"members\",\n+    \"levels\": [10, 50, 100, 250, 500, 1000]\n+  },\n+  \"held_fixed\": [\n+    \"Model: ecmwf/aifs-ens-1.0 (N320, 0.25 deg, 13 levels)\",\n+    \"Lead times: 6-hourly steps 0-360 h (15 days)\",\n+    \"Variables: 10 m wind, 2 m temperature, 24 h total precipitation\",\n+    \"Scoring: ERA5 1991-2020 seasonal per-gridpoint climatology, top-1% and top-0.1% thresholds\",\n+    \"7 initialization dates, 50 IFS-ENS perturbed initial conditions x 20 stochastic draws each\"\n+  ],\n+  \"predictions\": {\n+    \"if_lever\": \"Skill on top-percentile wind, temperature, and rain keeps rising past 50 members: 1,000 members sharpen the tails and improve extreme-event scores.\",\n+    \"if_not\": \"Skill flattens near 50 members: members are exchangeable draws of one trained distribution, so shared model error caps tail sharpness and extra members add nothing.\",\n+    \"decision_rule\": \"if_lever if extreme-event Brier/fair-CRPS skill at 1,000 members beats 50 members by >= 0.01 and still rises to 1,000; if_not if the gain past 100 members is < 0.005 (flat within the bootstrap confidence interval).\",\n+    \"noise_rule\": \"Bootstrap over which members are sampled and over the 7 dates; a real difference exceeds the 95% paired confidence interval, and the fair-CRPS correction separates genuine tail information from finite-ensemble-size bias.\",\n+    \"expected\": \"if_lever\",\n+    \"expected_why\": \"A 50-member estimate of a top-percentile probability carries roughly 1/sqrt(50) sampling error that 1,000 members reduces threefold, and HENS showed huge ensembles sample tails better.\"\n+  },\n+  \"compute_tested\": \"yes\",\n+  \"compute_tested_why\": \"The test varies ensemble size (members per forecast), which is exactly what more parallel GPUs buy: more members in the same wall time.\",\n+  \"scored_against\": \"ERA5 reanalysis (independent truth the model was not fit to produce for these forecast dates) and SYNOP station observations, for top-percentile 10 m wind, 2 m temperature, and 24 h precipitation.\",\n+  \"arms\": [\n+    {\"id\": \"a_small10\", \"what\": \"10-member ensemble (subsample)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"a_op50\", \"what\": \"50-member ensemble (ECMWF operational size)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"a_big1000\", \"what\": \"1,000-member ensemble (subsample)\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"baseline\": {\n+    \"what\": \"ECMWF operational AIFS-ENS: 50 perturbed members plus one control member\",\n+    \"value\": 50,\n+    \"source_id\": \"s_ecmwf_50\"\n+  },\n+  \"anchor\": {\n+    \"what\": \"Reproduce the published 4-minute N320 member time and 38 GB memory; one control run must match ECMWF open data within ensemble spread [s_crps_paper].\",\n+    \"published_value\": \"4 min per N320 member on A100 40 GB; 38 GB GPU memory\",\n+    \"tolerance\": \"timing within +/-25% of 4 min; 38 GB memory fits; control field within the ensemble's own member-to-member spread at each lead time (GPUs are non-deterministic, so exact reproduction is not expected)\",\n+    \"source_id\": \"s_crps_paper\",\n+    \"independent_code\": \"ECMWF Open Data AIFS ENS control member fields for the same initialization date, compared field-by-field\"\n+  },\n+  \"checks\": [\n+    \"One control-member 15-day forecast tracks the ECMWF open data AIFS ENS control within the ensemble's own spread.\",\n+    \"Rank histogram of the 1,000-member ensemble against ERA5 is near-uniform (calibration sanity).\",\n+    \"Fair CRPS at N=1000 converges to raw CRPS at N=1000 (size correction implemented correctly).\",\n+    \"ERA5 climatology threshold yields ~1% of grid-point-days above the top-1% threshold.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"phases\": [\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"p_pilot\",\n+      \"what\": \"Set up anemoi-inference on one A100 40 GB, run and time a few members, verify 38 GB memory and ~4 min/member, anchor one control run to ECMWF open data.\",\n+      \"stop_rule\": \"10 GPU-hour time box, or stop when timing and anchor both pass.\",\n+      \"gate\": {\n+        \"on\": \"n_infer_min_member\",\n+        \"op\": \"<=\",\n+        \"value\": 10,\n+        \"else\": \"re-plan: reduce members-per-date to 500 and double dates to hold the budget\"\n+      }\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"p_era5\",\n+      \"what\": \"Download ERA5 verification fields and compute per-gridpoint seasonal climatology thresholds (1991-2020).\",\n+      \"stop_rule\": \"done when all 7 dates and climatology are local\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"p_main\",\n+      \"what\": \"Generate 7 dates x 1,000 members (7,000 fifteen-day forecasts) on the 8-GPU A100 instance, streaming scores to disk.\",\n+      \"stop_rule\": \"finish all 7,000 members, or the budget_usd hard stop\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"p_score\",\n+      \"what\": \"Subsample each date's 1,000 members to 10/50/100/250/500/1,000; compute fair CRPS and Brier score vs N with bootstrap confidence intervals.\",\n+      \"stop_rule\": \"6 GPU-hour time box\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"p_station\",\n+      \"what\": \"Verify top-percentile events against SYNOP station observations (stretch).\",\n+      \"stop_rule\": \"4 GPU-hour time box\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"numbers\": [\n+    {\"id\": \"n_op_members\", \"name\": \"ECMWF operational AIFS-ENS ensemble size\", \"unit\": \"members\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 50, \"source_id\": \"s_ecmwf_50\", \"quote\": \"AIFS ENS currently has 50 perturbed members and one control member.\", \"page_setting\": \"ECMWF AIFS ENS operational configuration\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_infer_min_member\", \"name\": \"AIFS-CRPS N320 15-day per-member inference time\", \"unit\": \"min\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 4, \"source_id\": \"s_crps_paper\", \"quote\": \"a single member 15 day forecast is created in about one minute for AIFS-CRPS O96 and four minutes for AIFS-CRPS N320 on an NVIDIA A100 40 GB GPU, including the time spent reading the initial state and writing the forecast to disk.\", \"page_setting\": \"AIFS-CRPS N320 (0.25 deg, same grid as public AIFS-ENS v1) on NVIDIA A100 40 GB\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_mem_gb\", \"name\": \"AIFS-ENS v1 default GPU memory\", \"unit\": \"GB\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 38, \"source_id\": \"s_hf\", \"quote\": \"`aifs-ens-1.0` requires `38GB` of GPU memory by default, it is possible to reduce this by setting `ANEMOI_INFERENCE_NUM_CHUNKS` to a multiple of 2.\", \"page_setting\": \"ecmwf/aifs-ens-1.0 Hugging Face model card\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_lead_hours\", \"name\": \"AIFS-ENS forecast range\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 360, \"source_id\": \"s_ecmwf_dataset\", \"quote\": \"6 hourly steps to 360 (15 days)\", \"page_setting\": \"ECMWF AIFS ENS open data product description\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_step_hours\", \"name\": \"AIFS-ENS timestep\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 6, \"source_id\": \"s_ecmwf_dataset\", \"quote\": \"6 hourly steps to 360 (15 days)\", \"page_setting\": \"ECMWF AIFS ENS open data product description\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_rollout_steps\", \"name\": \"rollout steps per member\", \"unit\": \"steps\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_lead_hours / n_step_hours\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_hens_members\", \"name\": \"HENS (SFNO) ensemble size\", \"unit\": \"members\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 7424, \"source_id\": \"s_hens\", \"quote\": \"we generate a huge ensemble (HENS), with 7424 members initialized each day of summer 2023\", \"page_setting\": \"HENS Part 2 (SFNO-BVMC, 15-day, 0.25 deg)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_members_per_date\", \"name\": \"members generated per date\", \"unit\": \"members/date\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 1000},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_dates\", \"name\": \"initialization dates\", \"unit\": \"dates\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 7},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_total_members\", \"name\": \"total member forecasts\", \"unit\": \"members\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_members_per_date * n_dates\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_member_hours\", \"name\": \"per-member GPU time\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_infer_min_member / 60\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_total_gpu_hours\", \"name\": \"total GPU-hours\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_total_members * n_member_hours\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_gpus\", \"name\": \"GPUs in main instance\", \"unit\": \"GPU\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 8},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_a100_usd_h\", \"name\": \"A100 40 GB on-demand price\", \"unit\": \"USD/GPU-h\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 1.99, \"source_id\": \"s_lambda\", \"quote\": \"8x Instances pricing: NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR $1.99*\", \"page_setting\": \"Lambda on-demand pricing, 8x A100 SXM 40 GB\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_main_usd\", \"name\": \"main-run cost\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_total_gpu_hours * n_a100_usd_h\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_wall_hours\", \"name\": \"main-run wall time\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_total_gpu_hours / n_gpus\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_storage_gib\", \"name\": \"peak filesystem usage\", \"unit\": \"GiB\", \"basis\": \"GUESS\", \"value\": 100, \"rests_on\": \"aifs-ens checkpoint (~4 GB) plus ERA5 climatology and 7 verification dates (~20 GB) plus transient member GRIB buffered before streaming scores\", \"measured_by\": \"p_pilot\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_wall_days\", \"name\": \"filesystem held\", \"unit\": \"days\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 4},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_storage_usd\", \"name\": \"storage cost\", \"unit\": \"USD\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_storage_gib * fs_usd_gib_month * n_wall_days / 30\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_pilot_hours\", \"name\": \"pilot time box\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 10},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_score_hours\", \"name\": \"scoring time box\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 6},\n+    {\"id\": \"n_station_hours\", \"name\": \"station-check time box\", \"unit\": \"h\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 4}\n+  ],\n+  \"cost\": {\n+    \"rates\": [\n+      {\"id\": \"r_a100_1\", \"gpu\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM\", \"gpu_memory_gb\": 40, \"n_gpus\": 1, \"per_gpu_usd_h\": 1.99},\n+      {\"id\": \"r_a100_8\", \"gpu\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM\", \"gpu_memory_gb\": 40, \"n_gpus\": 8, \"per_gpu_usd_h\": 1.99}\n+    ],\n+    \"lines\": [\n+      {\"id\": \"L_pilot\", \"phase\": \"p_pilot\", \"what\": \"One A100 40 GB: install anemoi-inference, time ~2 members, verify 38 GB and ~4 min, anchor one control run\", \"kind\": \"allotment\", \"rate\": \"r_a100_1\", \"hours\": \"n_pilot_hours\", \"need\": 5},\n+      {\"id\": \"L_main\", \"phase\": \"p_main\", \"what\": \"Eight A100 40 GB: 7 dates x 1,000 members = 7,000 fifteen-day forecasts (466.7 total GPU-hours = 58.3 wall hours)\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100_8\", \"hours\": \"n_total_gpu_hours\"},\n+      {\"id\": \"L_score\", \"phase\": \"p_score\", \"what\": \"One A100 40 GB (CPU): subsample, fair CRPS + Brier vs N, bootstrap confidence intervals\", \"kind\": \"allotment\", \"rate\": \"r_a100_1\", \"hours\": \"n_score_hours\", \"need\": 3},\n+      {\"id\": \"L_storage\", \"phase\": \"p_score\", \"what\": \"Filesystem for checkpoint, ERA5, and transient GRIB\", \"kind\": \"storage\", \"usd\": \"n_storage_usd\"},\n+      {\"id\": \"L_station\", \"phase\": \"p_station\", \"what\": \"SYNOP station verification of top-percentile events\", \"kind\": \"allotment\", \"rate\": \"r_a100_1\", \"hours\": \"n_station_hours\", \"need\": 2, \"optional\": true}\n+    ],\n+    \"scenarios\": [\n+      {\"id\": \"sc_pessimistic\", \"what\": \"Per-member time doubles to 8 min: main cost ~$1,857, so halve dates to stay under budget\", \"set\": {\"n_infer_min_member\": 8}},\n+      {\"id\": \"sc_optimistic\", \"what\": \"3 min per member: afford 10 dates at 1,000 members\", \"set\": {\"n_infer_min_member\": 3, \"n_dates\": 10}}\n+    ],\n+    \"yields\": [\"n_total_members\", \"n_dates\"],\n+    \"spend_cap_usd\": 1000,\n+    \"total_stated\": 963.18\n+  },\n+  \"full_scale\": [\n+    {\"id\": \"f_hens_ai\", \"what\": \"One AIFS-ENS date at HENS size (7,424 members) - about the whole budget\", \"usd\": \"n_hens_members * n_member_hours * n_a100_usd_h\", \"ratio_to\": \"n_main_usd\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"f_reforecast\", \"what\": \"A 30-date multi-season reforecast at 1,000 members\", \"usd\": \"30 * n_members_per_date * n_member_hours * n_a100_usd_h\", \"ratio_to\": \"n_main_usd\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"outside_budget\": [\n+    {\"what\": \"engineer time (design, data prep, scoring, writeup)\", \"qty\": 3, \"unit\": \"person-days\"},\n+    {\"what\": \"ECMWF Open Data, ERA5, and SYNOP data access\", \"qty\": 0, \"unit\": \"USD (free under open data licenses)\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"restructuring\": {\n+    \"sequential_part\": \"Each member's 60 six-hour autoregressive steps; 7,000 members across 7 dates.\",\n+    \"method\": \"none\"\n+  },\n+  \"scope_gap\": [\n+    \"Multi-season or multi-year reforecast generality (only 7 dates).\",\n+    \"AIFS-ENS v2 or other ML models.\",\n+    \"Subseasonal (beyond 15-day) extremes.\",\n+    \"HENS-scale 7,424-member AIFS run (~$985/date, one date costs about the whole budget).\"\n+  ],\n+  \"novelty\": {\n+    \"closest_prior\": \"HENS Part 2: 7,424 SFNO members per day for 92 summer-2023 dates; showed huge ensembles sample 4-sigma tails and reduce outliers.\",\n+    \"closest_source_id\": \"s_hens\",\n+    \"prior_max_level\": 7424,\n+    \"left_open\": \"Whether AIFS-ENS, whose members are exchangeable draws of one afCRPS-trained distribution, keeps gaining skill past 50 members or saturates from shared model error.\",\n+    \"decides\": \"partly\",\n+    \"searched\": true\n+  },\n+  \"limits\": [\n+    \"Applies to AIFS-ENS v1 medium-range extremes on 7 dates; not a multi-season reforecast, other models, subseasonal leads, or direct proof that shared error causes any saturation.\"\n+  ],\n+  \"test_summary\": \"Run 7,000 fifteen-day AIFS-ENS v1 forecasts (7 dates x 1,000 members) on eight A100 40 GB GPUs; subsample 10-1,000 members, score top-percentile wind/temperature/rain probabilities against ERA5 with fair CRPS and Brier scores, and test whether skill still rises past 50 members.\",\n+  \"sources\": [\n+    {\"id\": \"s_hf\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/ecmwf/aifs-ens-1.0\", \"quote\": \"`aifs-ens-1.0` requires `38GB` of GPU memory by default, it is possible to reduce this by setting `ANEMOI_INFERENCE_NUM_CHUNKS` to a multiple of 2.\", \"supports\": \"GPU memory requirement for the public AIFS-ENS v1 weights (n_mem_gb)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_crps_paper\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.15832\", \"quote\": \"a single member 15 day forecast is created in about one minute for AIFS-CRPS O96 and four minutes for AIFS-CRPS N320 on an NVIDIA A100 40 GB GPU, including the time spent reading the initial state and writing the forecast to disk.\", \"supports\": \"per-member inference time at the exact N320 grid on the exact GPU (n_infer_min_member) and the anchor timing\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_ecmwf_50\", \"url\": \"https://www.ecmwf.int/sites/default/files/elibrary/102025/81687-aifs-ens-becomes-operational.pdf\", \"quote\": \"AIFS ENS currently has 50 perturbed members and one control member.\", \"supports\": \"the operational 50-member baseline (n_op_members, baseline)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_ecmwf_dataset\", \"url\": \"https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets/aifs-forecast-aifs-ensemble-set-x-aifs-ens\", \"quote\": \"6 hourly steps to 360 (15 days)\", \"supports\": \"15-day range and 6-hourly timestep (n_lead_hours, n_step_hours, n_rollout_steps)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_hens\", \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/18/5605/2025/\", \"quote\": \"we generate a huge ensemble (HENS), with 7424 members initialized each day of summer 2023\", \"supports\": \"the closest prior's ensemble size (n_hens_members, novelty)\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_forum\", \"url\": \"https://forum.ecmwf.int/t/inference-with-aifs-ens-v-1-on-s2s-timescales/14832\", \"quote\": \"AIFS-ENS was trained to minimise errors on medium-range timescales (up to ~10 days) and does not generalise well beyond that\", \"supports\": \"limit: model is trained for medium-range, so results are about 15-day medium-range extremes, not subseasonal\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_ems\", \"url\": \"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EMS2026/EMS2026-212.html\", \"quote\": \"It allows to define extremes using both percentile-based thresholds derived from the SYNOP station climatology or fixed absolute thresholds\", \"supports\": \"the percentile/SYNOP-climatology definition of extremes used for scoring\"},\n+    {\"id\": \"s_lambda\", \"url\": \"https://lambda.ai/pricing\", \"quote\": \"8x Instances pricing: NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR $1.99*\", \"supports\": \"the $1.99/GPU-h A100 40 GB on-demand rate (n_a100_usd_h, cost.rates)\"}\n+  ],\n+  \"files_read\": [\n+    \"https://huggingface.co/ecmwf/aifs-ens-1.0\",\n+    \"https://forum.ecmwf.int/t/inference-with-aifs-ens-v-1-on-s2s-timescales/14832\",\n+    \"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EMS2026/EMS2026-212.html\",\n+    \"https://eesm.science.energy.gov/sites/default/files/Fri_Mahesh_HugeEnsembles.pdf\",\n+    \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.15832\",\n+    \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/18/5605/2025/\",\n+    \"https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets/aifs-forecast-aifs-ensemble-set-x-aifs-ens\",\n+    \"https://www.ecmwf.int/sites/default/files/elibrary/102025/81687-aifs-ens-becomes-operational.pdf\",\n+    \"https://confluence.ecmwf.int/spaces/FCST/pages/540554034/Implementation+of+AIFS+ENS+v1\",\n+    \"https://huggingface.co/ecmwf/aifs-ens-2.0\",\n+    \"https://lambda.ai/pricing\"\n+  ]\n+}\n",
